# travl configuration — copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you have.
#
# Every value here is optional. With none of them set the app runs on
# OpenStreetMap tiles and a bundled place index: search, the itinerary, the
# map, sharing and print all work. Keys upgrade search quality, real photos
# and true driving directions.
#
# NOTE: anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the client bundle and is
# readable by anyone who loads the page. That is unavoidable for browser map
# SDKs — both Google and Amap work this way. Protect these with referrer and
# domain restrictions in the provider console, and set quota alerts. Do not
# put a server-side secret here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps — worldwide. Unreachable from mainland China.
# Enable: Maps JavaScript API, Places API (New), Routes API, Static Maps API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
# Optional. Static Maps is a separate REST endpoint, so it can take its own
# key with a tighter restriction. Falls back to the key above.
VITE_GOOGLE_STATIC_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Amap / 高德地图 — mainland China, Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan.
# Register at https://console.amap.com. The JS API key and the Web service
# key are two SEPARATE credentials; you need both for maps plus static images.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_AMAP_JS_KEY=
# Newer Amap JS accounts issue a security code alongside the JS key.
VITE_AMAP_SECURITY_CODE=
# Web service key — used by the static map endpoint for print.
VITE_AMAP_WEB_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign in with Google — for the scheduling page at #/meet.
#
# One OAuth 2.0 *Web application* client id, from
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials, with the Google Calendar
# API enabled. Add your origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) to both
# "Authorized JavaScript origins" and the OAuth consent screen.
#
# No client secret is involved: this is the browser token flow, which is what
# lets travl stay a static site. Signing in names you on your booking page and
# mirrors your published slots into a calendar you choose. Everything else —
# publishing times, taking bookings, adding to a guest's calendar — works with
# this left blank.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live collaboration relay.
#
# The scheduling page needs this for a booking link to reach anybody else:
# without it, a meet page lives in the browser that created it.
# Leave blank to keep trips local to the browser and share them by link.
# Set it to edit the same trip with other people in real time:
#   npm run relay
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_RELAY_URL=
